{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402681-time-travel-tremere","id":1402681,"title":"Time Travel Tremere","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-13T14:18:44-07:00","id":1402681,"title":"Time Travel Tremere","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> What is stopping a Tremere (or any other soul eating mage) with enough Time, from taking a soul, consuming/digesting it, and time travelling 1 hour before the act? Wouldnt they get all the benefits and the victim would not even be affected?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 07-13-2020, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T15:07:55-07:00","id":1402691,"title":"","content":"I thought in 1E Mage, Time Travel cannot be used to bring people back from the dead, but I guess that isn't the case in 2E? So how that interacts with souls is also a query of mine but I've held back on asking it for one reason or another. So I guess now I'd ask the same thing regarding this topic, since how souls interact with Time Travel is important for more than just Tremere double-dipping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T19:14:55-07:00","id":1402715,"title":"","content":"Nothing, really.<br /> <br /> Not unless the temporal shift locking in ripped the soul back out of the Tremere or their victim, even without the &quot;proper&quot; effects occurring. That doesn't really mesh well with RAW, but there are indications that certain effects transcend time. Perhaps this is one of the ways that soulless (or hollow) people can &quot;spontaneously&quot; form. If you go that way, it gets weird, but in a way that unlocks some interesting mysteries to investigate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T20:01:41-07:00","id":1402718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402681-time-travel-tremere#post1402681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is stopping a Tremere (or any other soul eating mage) with enough Time, from taking a soul, consuming/digesting it, and time travelling 1 hour before the act?</div> </div> </div> </div>For anything that's not the Tremere or a Reaper Legacy, there's the explicit statement in Shifting Sands that spells you've cast on things other than yourself in the undone time are undone, as well as Corridors of Time working in a manner that precludes taking anything back with you besides information; given that relevant Attainments are derived from the same principles as spells I don't see much reason to have them interact with time differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T20:51:44-07:00","id":1402727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402681-time-travel-tremere?p=1402718#post1402718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For anything that's not the Tremere or a Reaper Legacy, there's the explicit statement in Shifting Sands that spells you've cast on things other than yourself in the undone time are undone, as well as Corridors of Time working in a manner that precludes taking anything back with you besides information; given that relevant Attainments are derived from the same principles as spells I don't see much reason to have them interact with time differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but what does that mean for the process of soul-eating? Would it be like eating food? i.e. You go to a restaurant, eat a full meal, cast Shifting Sands with 1-hour reach, and suddenly you have not paid, but you are full (since you have eaten a meal). You go to a place, eat a full soul, cast Shifting Sands with 1-hour reach, and suddenly you have not harmed anyone, but you are replenished (since you have eaten a soul).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T21:16:41-07:00","id":1402730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402681-time-travel-tremere?p=1402727#post1402727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, but what does that mean for the process of soul-eating? Would it be like eating food? i.e. You go to a restaurant, eat a full meal, cast Shifting Sands with 1-hour reach, and suddenly you have not paid, but you are full (since you have eaten a meal). You go to a place, eat a full soul, cast Shifting Sands with 1-hour reach, and suddenly you have not harmed anyone, but you are replenished (since you have eaten a soul).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tremere have an entire game mechanic for dropping their rate of upkeep through inactivity, feed the Hollow at their cores in sympathy with the cosmic oversoul, can &quot;consume a soul&quot; without destroying it through normal use, and believe that the Gross Arcana \u2014 including Time \u2014 are less rarefied forms of the Subtle Arcana and that the paired divisions these form are themselves false constraints upon the true nature of reality that their Seventh Watchtower holds sway over.<br /> <br /> What I am saying is that it would be unthematic as hell for them to be so entropically-aspected and then be able to have a soul and eat it too through basic time-travel. Maybe some House might have figured out a way to e.g. parasitize souls through Fate-bound time loops and maintain a more stable equilibrium as part of a particular Mystery, but normal turn-back-the-clock-to-before-I-burned-a-human-soul use of the Arcana should not be allowed to break the basics of the soul economy out of hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}